From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruhan van der Berg <35257374+RuhanSA079@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:29:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] spi: rapuyama: polled driver for the RapuYama SPI controller

The RapuYama has three identical SPI controllers (0x20020400, 0x20020600,
0x20020a00, spi1/2/3.dll in the firmware) plus a block shared by them at
0x20020800. On the N8 the TI WL1271 WLAN chip sits on the second one.

Reversed from spi1/2/3.dll of the N8 RM-596 firmware: frame size and
padding, clock divider (sclk = 192 MHz / 2 / (div + 1)), clock polarity
and edge, fifo levels and thresholds, the settings handshake, the soft
reset and the per chip select release bits. Clocks are PowerResourceManager
resource 0x1c (cgc gate 0x0c) and resource 0x0b, which is a plain enable
bit in the shared block. The firmware does not touch the pin mux.

The driver is polled and half duplex like the firmware's polled engine,
which the WLAN uses: a write phase (TX FIFO writes, wait for room, wait
until idle) and a read phase in which every RXDATA read starts the next
frame (one dummy read starts the first, ENABLE = 2 keeps the last read
from starting another). 32 bit words are sent as two 16 bit frames, high
half first, which is what wlcore's WSPI expects. The divider is 10 bits.
Nothing is touched before probe, the shared clock enable is left on.
Probe also does the firmware's initial sync and its writes of the
controller bit to the shared block (0x810/0x82c/0x834).

For the bring-up the FIFO access width (io32, default 16 bit like the
firmware), the RXEN value (rxen, default 0) and a register dump around
the first frames (debug=N) are module parameters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/spi/Kconfig        |  11 +
 drivers/spi/Makefile       |   1 +
 drivers/spi/spi-rapuyama.c | 520 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 532 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/spi/spi-rapuyama.c

